{"title":"Determine If A Cell Is Reachable At A Given Time","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given four integers sx, sy, fx, fy, and a non-negative integer t.\nIn an infinite 2D grid, you start at the cell (sx, sy). Each second, you must move to any of its adjacent cells.\nReturn true if you can reach cell (fx, fy) after exactly t seconds, or false otherwise. If the start and finish are the same cell, reaching it after exactly one second is impossible.\nA cell's adjacent cells are the 8 cells around it that share at least one corner with it. You can visit the same cell several times.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: sx = 2, sy = 4, fx = 7, fy = 7, t = 6\nOutput: true\n```\nExplanation: Starting at cell (2, 4), we can reach cell (7, 7) in exactly 6 seconds by going through the cells depicted in the picture above. \n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: sx = 3, sy = 1, fx = 7, fy = 3, t = 3\nOutput: false\n```\nExplanation: Starting at cell (3, 1), it takes at least 4 seconds to reach cell (7, 3) by going through the cells depicted in the picture above. Hence, we cannot reach cell (7, 3) at the third second.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= sx, sy, fx, fy <= 10^9\n- 0 <= t <= 10^9\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def isReachableAtTime(self, sx: int, sy: int, fx: int, fy: int, t: int) -> bool:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().isReachableAtTime","parameters":[{"name":"sx","type":"int"},{"name":"sy","type":"int"},{"name":"fx","type":"int"},{"name":"fy","type":"int"},{"name":"t","type":"int"}],"returnType":"bool","tests":[{"input":[1,1,1,1,1],"expected":false},{"input":[10004843,774838665,515839028,977004155,713189009],"expected":true},{"input":[101823754,663968656,858351977,268979134,976832602],"expected":true},{"input":[105748441,506143170,35506170,165648135,976091318],"expected":true},{"input":[106010997,887195351,821886420,165136856,444542908],"expected":false},{"input":[106193890,185302257,786929281,445237512,267118725],"expected":f